---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Steve Wang - Project Hub"
  description="Steve Wang builds software, automation, and procurement systems for reporting, operations, and supply chain workflows."
>
  <main>
    <section class="hero section-wrap">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <h1>Steve Wang</h1>
        <div class="role-stack" aria-label="Primary disciplines">
          <span>Full-Stack Developer</span>
          <span>Data &amp; Process Automation</span>
          <span>Procurement Systems</span>
        </div>
        <p>
          I build full-stack software and practical automation tools, with experience
          across digital signage platforms, payments, CI/CD, and foodservice purchasing workflows.
        </p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="/projects/">View projects</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="/experience/">Experience</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="focus-panel" aria-label="Current focus summary">
        <div>
          <span>Production background</span>
          <strong>Digital signage CMS, payments, CI/CD, editor and template systems.</strong>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span>Live personal products</span>
          <strong>Fuel Tracker and Shared Bill on AWS, StackVitals for project operations, and the local-first QuotaStation Windows app.</strong>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span>Current build focus</span>
          <strong>Ordering Dashboard for purchasing and weekly reporting, alongside multi-provider quota monitoring in QuotaStation.</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-wrap section-block">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2>Featured Projects</h2>
        <a href="/projects/">All projects</a>
      </div>
      <div class="project-grid">
        <article class="project-card">
          <div class="project-meta">Full-stack product</div>
          <h3>Digital Signage CMS</h3>
          <p>CMS work across permissions, Stripe payments, CI/CD, templates, and built-in editing.</p>
          <a href="/projects/#digital-signage-cms">Read project notes</a>
        </article>
        <article class="project-card">
          <div class="project-meta">Open-source dashboard</div>
          <h3>StackVitals</h3>
          <p>Self-hosted operations dashboard for side projects — uptime, deploy health, cloud cost, AI/CI usage, and domain status in one lightweight view.</p>
          <a href="/projects/#stackvitals">View project</a>
        </article>
        <article class="project-card">
          <div class="project-meta">Private Windows app</div>
          <h3>QuotaStation</h3>
          <p>Local-first quota, reset, token, and cost monitoring for Codex and Claude Code, with tray, taskbar, dashboard, and status-line surfaces.</p>
          <a href="/projects/#quotastation">View project</a>
        </article>
        <article class="project-card">
          <div class="project-meta">Personal product</div>
          <h3>Fuel Tracker</h3>
          <p>Fuel logging with AI receipt extraction, shipped as a cloud web app and a portable desktop build with English/Chinese UI.</p>
          <a href="/projects/#fuel-tracker">Read project notes</a>
        </article>
        <article class="project-card">
          <div class="project-meta">Personal web app</div>
          <h3>Shared Bill</h3>
          <p>Shared expense tracker with sign-in, groups with member roles and invites, weighted splits, settlement calculation, and completed transfers.</p>
          <a href="/projects/#shared-bill">Read project notes</a>
        </article>
        <article class="project-card">
          <div class="project-meta">Purchasing workflow app</div>
          <h3>Ordering Dashboard</h3>
          <p>Desktop purchasing app with Excel/ODS import, committed-order tracking, supplier and item rules, cycle-aware recommendations, and grouped export.</p>
          <a href="/projects/#purchasing-workflow-tools">View scope</a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-wrap shipped-section" aria-label="Recently shipped releases">
      <div class="shipped-card">
        <span class="shipped-title">Recently shipped</span>
        <ul class="shipped-list">
          <li>
            <span class="shipped-version">v1.6.0</span>
            <a href="/projects/#shared-bill">Shared Bill</a>
            <p>Completed the hosted backend migration from Supabase to serverless AWS.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="shipped-version">v1.3.0</span>
            <a href="/projects/#purchasing-workflow-tools">Ordering Dashboard</a>
            <p>Sales-order commitments, all-status PO tracking, configurable groups, and styled low-stock exports.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="shipped-version">v1.0.0</span>
            <a href="/lab/#weekly-sales-reporting">Weekly Report Manager</a>
            <p>First tagged release of the desktop reporting app already used for the weekly sales cycle.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="shipped-version">v0.2.0</span>
            <a href="/projects/#quotastation">QuotaStation</a>
            <p>Cross-provider status line, taskbar quick-panel trigger, and clearer quota-window reporting.</p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="proof-band">
      <div>
        <strong>Product Engineering</strong>
        <span>Full-stack CMS, payment, CRM, and deployment work</span>
      </div>
      <div>
        <strong>Automation</strong>
        <span>Python tools for reporting and purchasing workflows</span>
      </div>
      <div>
        <strong>Operations</strong>
        <span>Design from real purchasing and supply chain work</span>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
